WEBVTT

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.150
<i>The rip entry.</i>

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:18.780
<i>An entry into the water with no splash.</i>

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:24.640
<i>This is a key diving technique,
required to score points in diving competitions.</i>

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:31.380
<i>However, while we were standing beside the pool,
we were suddenly showered with an unbelievable statement.</i>

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:36.390
If none of you make it into the Olympics, then the club will be shut down.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:41.220
Do you think you boys are up for it?

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.390
You wanna make it to the Tokyo Olympics?

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:46.650
I do.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:50.080
<i>The Tokyo Olympics.</i>

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.680
<i>That was something far off in the distance, almost out of reach for me.</i>

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:02.570
<i>But strangely, the thought made really excited.</i>

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:30.410
See what no one else has ever seen

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:37.510
We'll start by having each of you do a dive for me.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.270
Okay, that's enough. You can come down.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:49.270
Huh?

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.490
There's no need to see you dive.

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:53.270
Just walk down the stairs.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.270
What the heck?

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.530
Okay, that's enough.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:03.530
Come back down.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.340
I want to dive...

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.210
Okay, okay. You're done.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.750
Get back down here.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:28.270
A diver who can't even stand with the proper form can't hope to execute a proper dive.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.150
Your neck is too tense.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.340
Bring your butt in more.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:41.770
Keep your arms straight.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:43.390
But keep them loose.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:46.160
Hold your fingers together, but don't tense them up.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.770
Relax your upper body,

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.100
and keep your lower body tight.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:54.040
Focus all your strength in the center of your abdomen.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:04:02.040
How long have you been diving that you
still don't know how to align your bodies?

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:08.030
<i>Body alignment is the proper posture when diving.</i>

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:12.440
<i>For example, if you drop grapes from the diving platform,</i>

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:16.960
<i>the center of gravity shifts all over the place, and it'll fall to the water unbalanced.</i>

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:23.200
<i>But a cucumber will fall in a straight line and cut through the water on entry.</i>

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.450
<i>Instead of dispersing your power throughout your body,</i>

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:31.110
<i>you pull your body in like a cucumber for your performance.</i>

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:33.960
<i>Those are the basics for a beautiful midair performance.</i>

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.960
<i>But that's not a good reason to
keep us standing here for an hour!</i>

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.530
Okay, that's all for the first half.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.840
We'll pick things back up here after a ten-minute break.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:52.030
That lady is crazy.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:58.370
I know body alignment is important,
but what idiot does it for an hour or two straight?

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.460
I think it could be a plan.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:04.110
Maybe she's being difficult on purpose since the beginning is so important.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:07.540
Yeah, there are people like that.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:11.330
It's always the unconfident ones
that use these unnecessary tricks.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.650
Yeah, there are people like that.

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:15.870
Youichi.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:20.140
I've met coaches like that too.

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:25.020
A male coach from America taught me in the same way that woman does.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:26.130
Yeah?

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.480
The first day was hammering in body alignment.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.410
The second day was dry practice.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:34.530
The third day was practicing the approach and footwork.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:39.150
And in the end, he didn't teach us anything about actual diving.

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:42.150
Everyone complained and complained.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.280
I bet.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:51.240
But after that coach went back to America,
we could finally see how much our diving improved.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.660
The Japanese coaches were shocked.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:58.340
Also, this was something we found out later,

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:03.170
but that man coached a diver who went on to win Olympic gold for America.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.420
I see.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.430
Wait, Youichi.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.930
Does that American coach have something to do with her?

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.200
No, not really.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:18.190
They just have similar coaching styles, that's all.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:22.440
Well, there does seem to be more to her than meets the eye.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.570
How can you tell?

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:28.820
They say you can spot a great diver by the way they stand on the platform.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.510
It's the same way with coaches.

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:34.250
You can just tell by looking at them poolside.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.460
She's got a nice butt, doesn't she?

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:44.710
It's not bad, I guess.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:53.100
There are a lot of Japanese divers who shy away from dives that require doing handstands on the platform.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.720
The reason is plainly a lack of practice.

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:56.910
Listen up.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:01.080
The muscles you need for handstands can only be worked by actually doing handstands.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.230
So I want you doing handstands every day.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.360
Whenever you're free, I want you in a handstand.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.860
Diving is a mental competition.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:16.490
If you get confident doing something everyone hates to do, then that'll always give you an edge during a competition.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.000
Okay, that's all for today.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:22.750
I thought I was going to throw up.

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:25.630
I thought my brains were going to leak from my ears.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:30.260
There's something I want to give you,
so wait for me in the lobby after you get changed.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.070
Got it.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:34.160
Sakai Tomoki, was it?

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:35.190
You have a minute?

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.270
How many years have you been diving?

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:40.640
A little over five.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:44.430
Has anybody ever told you that you were double-jointed?

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.770
What's that?

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:48.210
It means you're more flexible than average.

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:50.770
It's a body type that's suited for diving.

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:52.280
I'll put it plainly.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:55.100
There's no doubt you'll improve.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.410
So aim for the top.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:00.660
Climb to the highest peak you can.

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:05.420
Does that mean winning a spot
on the Japanese Olympic team?

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.390
You dream small, kid.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:10.100
I told you.

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:13.050
We've got our sights on the Olympics.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:16.960
You said you wanted to go too, didn't you?

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:19.560
I was just caught up in the moment.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:23.990
Well, if you've got the will, then continue to climb to the top.

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:27.570
There's a view only you can see.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:30.570
A view only I can see?

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:39.060
If that's something I'll get to see,
then I want to go to the Olympics.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:40.870
This time I'm serious.

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:43.380
I'm serious too.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.510
What did she want back there?

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.890
Oh, she mentioned something about being double-jointed.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:08:58.890
What's that?

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:00.640
Thanks for waiting.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.270
What is it that you wanted to give us?

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:05.640
This.

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:10.030
What is this?

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:12.150
It's your daily independent training regimen.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:16.780
Independent training? Isn't that voluntary?

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:21.160
But you Japanese kids won't do it unless you're told to.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.410
We do sometimes.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:26.050
Everybody does it sometimes.

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:28.670
Even the most mediocre of athletes.

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:35.190
Anyway, I'm sorry to do this after just starting here, but I'll be away on business all next week.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:37.430
Make sure you do your training while I'm gone.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:38.570
What?

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:39.800
What's that about?

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.070
Come in.

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:55.320
What is it?

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:03.540
Our new coach, Coach Asaki, will be focusing on the elementary and junior high students.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.200
Okay.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:08.460
Are you sure you're fine with me continuing to coach you?

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:11.730
I'm fine with how things are. It's just...

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:14.960
I'll do my dry practice with them.

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:17.130
Okay, got it.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:17.810
Thanks.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:20.090
Bye, then.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:32.940
Let's go, Chikuwa.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.110
This is for your own good.

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:39.990
Follow my instructions exactly, as if your life depended on it.

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:42.500
First, you need to jog every morning.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:46.000
If you've got a dog, run with them for at least an hour.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:50.120
You don't wear socks indoors, right?

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.560
Diving is a sport done barefoot.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:55.630
So why wouldn't you spend every moment getting used to it?

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:58.400
You need to work on your endurance.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:03.140
In order to ensure a sharp performance throughout a long competition,

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:07.630
you need muscles, concentration, and mental fortitude.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:11.900
Basic endurance is the foundation for all of that.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:15.900
And I'll keep repeating this:
You have to master body alignment.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:19.580
Check your posture every night in front of the mirror.

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.740
Are your shoulders tense?

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.420
Is your stomach sticking out?

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:25.160
Is your butt tight?

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.560
Tighten it up, huh?

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:28.770
Hey, Tomo.

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:29.790
What?!

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.790
Your phone's ringing.

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.830
Hello, did you call me?

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.430
<i>Oh, yeah.</i>

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:46.840
<i>You free today?</i>

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:50.010
<i>We're all talking about hanging out
somewhere since we have the day off.</i>

00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:51.690
Uh...

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:56.940
Warm-up

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:56.940
Jogging

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:56.940
Stretches

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:56.940
Weightlifting

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:56.940
Body alignment

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:56.940
Cool-down

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:54.260
<i>I bought a new game.</i>

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:56.520
Sorry, but I can't make it.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.860
<i>Diving again?</i>

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.950
<i>All right, it's fine. I'll just invite someone else.</i>

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:02.610
Maybe some other—

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:26.720
There he is.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:33.800
There's no mistake.

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:35.100
He's the one.

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:39.730
In other words, you're scared.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:41.240
Of what?

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:44.240
You're scared of parting with the ocean.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:47.740
You're scared of stepping into a new world.

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:53.000
And you're scared of ruining what your grandfather has built.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:54.870
What does that mean?

00:12:55.500 --> 00:13:00.450
Okitsu Shibuki, the grandson of the
legendary diving master Okitsu Shiraha.

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:02.490
You only dive in the ocean.

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:04.510
I'll admit that's cool.

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:10.170
There's no reason to risk moving to the pool,
like your grandfather.

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:14.020
Gramps didn't go to Tokyo to risk danger.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:18.290
He went hoping for something amazing.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:20.370
But there was nothing.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:24.030
Gramps had nothing left and nothing to leave behind.

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:25.530
He did.

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:30.580
Don't tell me he survives in people's memories or something.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:33.120
It doesn't matter if there's nothing to show for it.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.660
You lose if there aren't results you can see.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:40.420
Then I'll show you what your grandfather left behind.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:41.600
Huh?

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:47.360
But that's only if you can fulfill my grandfather's final wish.

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:51.430
What? Coach Asaki is?

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:57.940
Yeah. She's the granddaughter of MDC's late founder, Chairman Mizuki.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:13:59.810
And that's not all.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:02.070
Coach Asaki is a former diver,

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:05.570
and she apparently did quite well in her junior competitions.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:12.830
Let's see... She lived in New York for eight years,
between the ages of 6 and 14, which makes her a returnee.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:16.060
That's right, New York! We're talking New York!

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:18.830
That's not New York!

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:22.700
She started diving when she was eight.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:26.100
She took a break after returning to Japan,

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:32.220
but after graduating high school, she headed back to America alone to take up diving once again.

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:38.100
But this time, it wouldn't be as an athlete; she would be studying coaching instead.

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:40.480
Why do you think she did that?

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:41.960
No idea.

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.480
I don't know, why?

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:49.110
So she could coach here at MDC,
the club founded by her grandfather, Chairman Mizuki.

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:51.620
She did it just for that?

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:53.570
And also...

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:54.370
What?

00:14:54.700 --> 00:15:00.370
She's planning to send one of us to the Olympics to stop them from shutting MDC down.

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:02.380
She's serious?

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:06.640
We've got our sights on the Olympics.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:09.260
Does that mean we're trying for the Olympics?

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.180
That's impossible.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:12.260
Right?

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.770
What's with the negative attitude?

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:17.350
Is it really impossible?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.770
It isn't.

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:21.730
There's still 18 months until the Olympics.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.520
It's too early to give up.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.060
You're right.

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:27.120
I'm not sure about that.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:30.030
There might be a possibility for you, Youichi, but...

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:34.650
You're right, it might've been impossible if this were any other sport.

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:36.910
But diving is a shallow field.

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:40.620
There are three individual men's divers.

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:44.920
You could say that Hyogo's Teramoto
Ken'ichirou is guaranteed at this point.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.300
But the rest are a toss-up.

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:52.430
Yeah, well, we're not even in the mix with them, right?

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:54.430
Yeah.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.620
You guys are way too pessimistic.

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:59.680
You're the one that needs to look at reality the most.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.820
Speaking of reality,

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:06.340
if none of us make it to the Olympics,
then this club is going to be shut down.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:09.820
Oh, Youichi, you actually said it.

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:13.950
But we have that new coach.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:19.270
It'll be fine.

00:16:19.270 --> 00:16:22.600
There won't be a problem if Youichi makes it to the Olympics.

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:24.440
You're just leaving things to others.

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:26.590
That's just being realistic.

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:30.090
Is the possibility really zero?

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:31.620
For what?

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:34.090
For us to go to the Olympics.

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:35.600
It's not zero.

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:38.650
It's more like a negative chance.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:43.320
Anyway, you guys wanna grab some food on our way home?

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:44.180
Sounds good.

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:45.440
I'll go too.

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.530
Elementary school kids can't come.

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:49.860
Why not?

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:52.110
What about our individual training?

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:56.640
Individual training? Wait, don't tell me, Tomo...

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:58.490
You're actually doing it?

00:16:59.280 --> 00:16:59.990
Uh-huh.

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:01.420
Every day?

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:02.690
Yeah.

00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:06.180
Doesn't that basically eat up all your free time?

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:07.880
Yeah, it's been tough.

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:12.140
Well, then let's stop by the convenience store.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:13.510
We'll sprint.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.360
What, we're running?

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:16.760
It's for our training.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.430
That's a great idea.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:30.520
What, you're running again today?

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:31.280
Yeah.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:34.240
What's the point of getting all buff?

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:39.030
I mean, why is Miu dating such a dumb jock?

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:42.790
She'd be better off dating me over you.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:44.290
Tell her that.

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:45.790
I already have.

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:47.040
Huh?

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:52.550
Coach Asaki is back!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.420
And she's brought a man!

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:55.920
What?

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:57.930
It could be her lover!

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:08.940
All right, everyone, listen up.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:11.190
I've got someone I want to introduce.

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:13.700
L-L-Lo—

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:14.590
Here's my lover.

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:15.500
Okitsu.

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:21.450
This is Okitsu Shibuki, MDC's newest member.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:24.450
He's just moved to Tokyo from Aomori yesterday.

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:26.900
Come on, say hello.

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:28.710
Hello.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.580
Nice to meet you.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:33.090
All right, go back to your stretches.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:36.590
Did you do your individual training?

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:37.740
Yes.

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:38.840
I guess so.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:39.590
Yes.

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:42.360
It's fine. I'll be able to tell by looking.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:46.700
According to Coach Ooshima,

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:52.610
he's the grandson of Okitsu Shiraha,
who was once considered a diving master.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:55.110
They said he only dives in the ocean.

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:58.340
He doesn't talk much.

00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:00.300
Totally like a man of the sea.

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:03.230
Like he only opens up to fish?

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:08.240
More importantly, Sacchin,
is it true he's never dove in a pool before?

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:10.080
I think that's probably true.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:13.380
Although, I'm pretty sure him getting eaten by a whale is made up.

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:17.760
In that case, what made him want to dive in a pool now?

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:21.390
Everyone is curious about you.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:26.640
I bet you've never had people looking
forward to your diving with the ocean.

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:28.630
How does it feel?

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:31.150
Doesn't it give you butterflies?

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:32.590
Butterflies?

00:19:32.590 --> 00:19:37.630
Yes, your blood vessels become like the tide,
and your blood starts going crazy.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:41.910
You get filled with a feeling of power that
makes you believe that you can do anything.

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.890
It's not bad, is it?

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:47.790
I feel more annoyed than excited when I'm around you.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.540
So, what are you going to do?

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:51.520
I'm going home.

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.520
To where? Tsugaru?

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:56.290
What about your promise?

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:59.670
It wasn't a promise, it was a contract.

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:05.090
If you want me to honor my end of our contract, then you need to dive from there first.

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:07.310
Go dive.

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:09.040
Who the hell are you?

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:10.860
Fujitani Youichi.

00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:15.940
If someone in the diving world doesn't know me, then they've had their heads buried in the sand.

00:20:16.670 --> 00:20:19.360
Sorry. Guess I'm one of them.

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:22.910
You've been diving in the ocean waters of Tsugaru, right?

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:24.610
Get on the platform.

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:26.310
I want to see you dive.

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:37.960
What the heck? He's not diving at all.

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:41.760
It can't be that he's scared, right?

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.670
He's not used to it yet.

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:48.280
Not the flat platform, or the feel of the concrete.

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:49.710
Or even having an audience.

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:53.730
That's so high.

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:56.650
Whoa!

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:02.940
Zero points for the entry, though.

00:21:05.020 --> 00:21:09.580
<i>We'd never seen such a wild dive before.</i>

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:18.810
<i>What was the man who entered our lives with such a
large splash about to bring to my world, and to MDC?</i>
